\title{flexyBayes: Bayesian Mixed Models with ASReml Syntax, Powered by Greta and INLA}
\description{
\code{flexyBayes} lets you fit Bayesian mixed models using the formula syntax
you already know from ASReml or \code{lme4}/\code{brms}, dispatched through one of
two inference engines: greta (Hamiltonian Monte Carlo via TensorFlow) or
INLA (integrated nested Laplace approximation, for the latent Gaussian
model class). The same fitted object supports \code{summary()}, \code{predict()},
\code{emmeans::emmeans()}, \code{marginaleffects::predictions()}, and the
\verb{bayesplot::*} family.
}
\details{
The package's signature feature is \code{triangulate()}, a cross-engine
posterior comparison that quantifies disagreement between two fits of
the same model on the same data.
}
\section{Entry points}{

Two ingest paths share a single internal model representation
(\code{fb_terms}):
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=flexybayes]{flexybayes()}} — asreml-format entry: \code{fixed} / \code{random} / \code{rcov}
formulas, \code{known_matrices} for kinship / pedigree, \code{weights} for
pre-aggregated observations.
\item \code{\link[=fb]{fb()}} — brms-format entry: a single \code{formula} plus \code{backend}
(\code{"greta"}, \code{"inla"}, or \code{"auto"}).
\item \code{\link[=fb_prior]{fb_prior()}} — penalised-complexity-canonical prior DSL.
\item \code{\link[=triangulate]{triangulate()}} — cross-engine posterior comparison.
}
}

\section{Vignettes}{

Twelve vignettes ship with the package, covering: getting started,
asreml-shaped formulas reference, downstream analysis, backend
internals, priors and regularisation, cross-engine triangulation,
LGM feasibility, foundational regression, hierarchical models,
structured covariance, spatio-temporal, and multi-environment trials
and genomics.
}

